@page "/recipes/quiche-valerie"

<PageTitle>Quiche Valerie</PageTitle>

<div class="recipe-detail-page">
    <section class="recipe-hero">
        <div class="recipe-copy">
            <h1>Quiche Valerie</h1>

            <p>
                An elegant French-style baked custard tart loaded with roasted garlic, 
                tender vegetables, and a flaky buttery crust.
            </p>

            <div class="meta-row">
                <span class="meta-pill">
                    <span class="meta-icon">◔</span>
                    <span>Prep: 25 min</span>
                </span>
                <span class="meta-pill">
                    <span class="meta-icon">◔</span>
                    <span>Cook: 40 min</span>
                </span>
                <span class="meta-pill">
                    <span class="meta-icon">◔</span>
                    <span>Serves: 6-8</span>
                </span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="recipe-hero-image">
            <img src="images/quiche-valerie.jpg" alt="Honey fried chicken" />
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="scallop-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <section class="recipe-grid">
        <article class="info-card ingredients-card">
            <h2>
                <span class="list-mark"></span>
                Ingredients List
            </h2>

            <div class="ingredient-group">
                <ul>
                    <li>1 pre-baked 9-inch pie crust</li>
                    <li>4 large eggs</li>
                    <li>1 cup heavy cream</li>
                    <li>1 cup whole milk</li>
                    <li>1 cup shredded Gruyère or Swiss cheese</li>
                    <li>1/2 cup cooked bacon or diced ham</li>
                    <li>1/2 cup leeks or sweet onions, thinly sliced and sautéed until soft</li>
                    <li>Pinch of ground nutmeg, salt, and white pepper</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
            <h2>
                <span class="list-mark"></span>
                Step-by-Step Guide
            </h2>

            <ol>
                <li>Crank your oven to 190°C (375°F) and position an oven rack in the center position.</li>
                <li>Arrange your pre-baked pie crust on a baking sheet, then evenly scatter the cooked bacon or diced ham, sautéed leeks, and shredded Gruyère cheese directly across the bottom of the pastry shell.</li>
                <li>In a large mixing bowl, vigorously whisk together the 4 eggs, heavy cream, whole milk, ground nutmeg, salt, and white pepper for at least 2 full minutes until the liquid is completely uniform and a thin layer of foam forms on top.</li>
                <li>Slowly pour the custard mixture over the cheese and meats in the pie crust, allowing the liquid to settle naturally into all the gaps without disturbing the even layer of fillings.</li>
                <li>Place the baking sheet in the oven and bake for 35 to 40 minutes until the edges of the quiche are puffed up and golden-brown, but the exact center still maintains a slight, gelatinous wobble when the pan is nudged.</li>
                <li>Remove from the oven and let it sit on a wire rack until completely cool, then place it in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour; this setting period binds the egg proteins, allowing you to slice pristine, firm wedges that won't fall apart during transport.</li>
            </ol>
        </article>
    </section>
</div>
